# Mobile App – Expo Patterns

## Data layer: Legend-State → Supabase (no SQLite, no Drizzle, no TanStack Query for app data)

All synced data lives in Legend-State observables (`lib/store/index.ts`), persisted to MMKV and synced to Supabase via `syncedSupabase`. Never call the Supabase REST API directly for CRUD — mutate the observables.

```typescript
// Read (reactive) — components use the observable hooks
import { wallets$ } from '@/lib/store';
import { use$ } from '@legendapp/state/react';
const wallets = use$(wallets$);

// Write — via helpers in lib/supabase/*.ts which set() into the store;
// Legend-State syncs to Postgres in the background
wallets$[id].set({ ...wallet, name: 'Updated' });

// Delete — soft delete only (synced tables have a `deleted` column)
```

New synced table checklist: migration adds `created_at`/`updated_at`/`deleted` + RLS + realtime → add observable in `lib/store/index.ts` → CRUD helper in `lib/supabase/`.

## MMKV instances (lib/mmkv/)

- `auth` — Supabase session storage (client uses `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`)
- `legend-store` — observable persistence
- `image-uploads` — receipt upload queue
- `preferences` — local UI prefs (theme: light / dark / system; default wallet id cache for AI fallback)

## AI pipeline (lib/ai/)

Input → `processing-queue.ts` (MMKV) → `background-processor.ts` (Android FG service) → `run-extraction.ts` → `lib/ai/client` (HTTP → Go backend when `EXPO_PUBLIC_AI_API_URL` set, mock otherwise) → `lib/ai/routine.ts` (history match: routine notification → ledger directly, else category-prefilled `proposed_transactions` → the Review deck `app/review.tsx`, decisions in `lib/proposals/review-actions.ts`). Moni chat (`app/chat.tsx`) also routes finance Q&A via `lib/ai/chat/` → `/v1/chat/analyze`.

- Client results are `{ status: 'ok' | 'skipped' | 'unavailable' }` — never throw across this boundary
- Wire types in `lib/ai/client/types.ts` must match `apps/backend/internal/extract/types.go`
- Notification prefilter is on-device (`lib/notifications/notification-filter.core.js`). Headless-shared helpers: see rule `mobile-headless-js` (`*.core.js` + thin `*.ts`). Wallet–app linking: `notification_package` on wallets + MMKV linked-package cache; installed app labels/icons via `modules/moni-android-apps` (Android 11+ `<queries>` in module manifest + `plugins/with-notification-listener-manifest.js`; rebuild dev client after native/manifest changes).

## Routing (expo-router)

`app/(auth)` unauthenticated; `app/(tabs)` the four tab roots `index` (Home), `activity`, `budget`, `debts`; every other route is a pushed root Stack page with no tab bar, sliding in from the right: `chat` (Moni chat), `profile`, `wallet`, `transaction`, `review`, `budget`, `bill`, `categories`, `debt`, `capture`, `merchants`, `capture-sources`, `capture-log`, `debug`, `map`, `place`. Auth guard in `app/_layout.tsx`. Custom JS `Tabs` with the floating bar in `components/nav/tab-bar.tsx` (not NativeTabs); `TABS` there is the one list of tabs. The + opens the chooser sheet (`components/nav/capture-chooser.tsx`, sheet kind `chooser`), and each row pushes its page. A tab must not share its name with a root folder that has an `index`: `/budget` would open the folder's index, not the tab (`components/nav/__tests__/tab-bar.test.tsx` checks it). Push typed routes without `as never`. From a pushed page, reach a tab with `router.dismissTo`; `push` or `replace` to a tab stacks a second `(tabs)`.

## Styling (Uniwind)

Tailwind via Uniwind `className` — **not** NativeWind. Design tokens live in `global.css`:

- **Redesign v2 is in progress.** Before building or changing any screen, read [`docs/REDESIGN.md`](../../docs/REDESIGN.md): the canvas boards to build, [`docs/redesign/tokens.md`](../../docs/redesign/tokens.md) and [`docs/redesign/glossary.md`](../../docs/redesign/glossary.md). For new work it overrides the visual rules below.
- [`docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`](../../docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md) is the v1 visual source of truth. Follow its component hierarchy, native-currency, evidence, accessibility, and motion rules before inventing a new UI pattern.
- `@theme`: v2 radii (`rounded-card`, `rounded-tile`, `rounded-field`, `rounded-sheet`), spacing (`screen`, `section`, `card`, `bubble`, `touch`), and the Funnel Display families
- Semantic light/dark: v1 names (`canvas`, `card`, `foreground`, `muted`, `primary`, state tokens) mapped to v2 values, plus the v2 roles (`sand`, `hairline`, `ink-2`, `deep-mint`, pastels, `over`) in `@layer theme` `@variant`; edit `global.css` only, then `pnpm --filter moni gen:tokens`
- Text: import `Text` from `@/components/ui/text` (Funnel Display; ESLint rejects the `react-native` import); weight via `font-display-semibold` / `font-display-bold`, never `font-bold`
- Motion and haptics: springs from `lib/motion/tokens.ts`; haptics only through the moment functions in `lib/haptics` (ESLint rejects `expo-haptics` in `app/` and `components/`)
- Screens use semantic utilities (`bg-canvas`, `bg-card`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted`, `bg-primary`) — never hardcode brand hex
- JS color props (charts, tab bar, icons): `useThemeTokens()` from `@/hooks/use-theme-tokens`
- Theme preference: `lib/theme/preference.ts` → `Uniwind.setTheme('light' | 'dark' | 'system')`; default **light**
- Shared chrome: `components/ui/page` (every full-screen page), `press` (the only press primitive for new controls), `button`, `header-icon-button`, `form-field`, `chip`
- Every `Pressable`, `TextInput`, `Switch`, and v2 control gets `testID={tid('<screen>', ...parts)}` from `lib/test-ids.ts`; `pnpm --filter moni lint:test-ids` enforces it in CI.
- UI copy follows `docs/redesign/glossary.md`; `pnpm --filter moni lint:copy` fails on a banned word or format, and fixed v1 hits come off `scripts/lint/copy-allow.txt` (`--write` regenerates it).

## Receipt camera (Android)

`lib/receipts/scan-receipt.ts` (the chooser's Scan a receipt, `/capture/scan`, and the chat camera) calls `modules/moni-document-scanner` (Nitro) → Google ML Kit native document scanner, which is the camera stage of `/capture/scan`. Post-scan: `lib/receipts/normalize-scan.ts` (copy + 1024px cap). **Android only** — iOS shows an alert. Requires Google Play Services; rebuild dev client after native module changes (`npx expo run:android`).
